{"user": "What is a legal move? Meaning something has to flip?", "user_ts": "2026-08-21T13:22:54.482844+00:00", "assistant": "Yes \u2014 a legal move **must flip at least one opponent disc**.\n\nYou place a Black disc on an empty square only if, in at least one straight line \u2014 horizontal, vertical, or diagonal \u2014 it **brackets one or more White discs** between the new Black disc and an existing Black disc.\n\nSo if nothing flips, it\u2019s **not legal**. If you have **no legal moves at all**, you must **pass**.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-21T13:22:56.826969+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-21T13:22:58.007497+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle"], "consensus": ["General Principle"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3, "Positive Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0, "Positive Feedback": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle"], "llama": ["General Principle"], "sonnet": ["General Principle", "Positive Feedback"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}}
